# 19. LEAST PRIVILEGE

Users and services should have only the permissions required for their role.

Example:

```text
Web application
      ↓
Database
      ↓
Only required permissions
```

Not:

```text
Web application
      ↓
Database administrator
      ↓
Full database control
```

---

# 20. SECURE CODING REVISION

Important defenses:

| Vulnerability | Main Defense |
|---|---|
| SQL Injection | Parameterized queries |
| XSS | Context-appropriate output encoding |
| CSRF | CSRF tokens + SameSite/Origin controls |
| IDOR | Server-side authorization |
| Path Traversal | Canonicalization + allowlisting/safe IDs |
| Command Injection | Avoid shell + fixed arguments |
| SSRF | Destination validation/allowlisting + network controls |
| Weak passwords | Strong password hashing |
| Secrets exposure | Secret management |
| Excess privileges | Least privilege |

